& [CanonicalRecord: PostIR6ImplementationReadiness] is the processed planning authority for the post-IR6 implementation readiness surface
  + [canonical_uuid] is 082bb164-35fd-4339-8875-ae0931327210
  + [source_manifest_uuid] is 5cac4124-fcf3-4caa-9067-cdf670e004f0
  + [surface_uuid] is 4a2a8e2b-d10d-49d3-8aa7-41a77412a75b
  + [authority_scope] is post-IR6 IR7 readiness, final-slice minting authority, gating rules, model routing, forbidden scope, expected outputs, and verification obligations
  + [implementation_scope] is IR7 planning readiness authority only
  + [depends_on] is docs/planning/IR6_Coordination_Mailbox_Projection_Prototype_Implementation_Proof_Pack.v1.sop
  + [depends_on] is docs/reviews/IR6_Implementation_Completion_Review.v1.sop
  + [depends_on] is docs/planning/FSC5_Operations_Safety_Pack.v1.sop
  + [depends_on] is docs/canonical/LangSOP_Operations_Safety_Spec.canonical.sop
  + [depends_on] is docs/canonical/LangSOP_Post_FSC5_Implementation_Readiness.canonical.sop

  = must: use docs/planning/Post_IR6_Implementation_Readiness_Surface.v1.sop as the current post-IR6 readiness surface
  = must: mint IR7 final slices before writing operations simulator code, fixture files, expected ledgers, generated outputs, dependencies, adapters, transports, or package metadata
  = must: preserve accepted IR6 proof and FSC5 operations safety as boundary inputs
  = must: preserve that post-IR6 readiness does not authorize operations simulator implementation, agent dispatch, operations control, or live machine control
  - never: treat post-IR6 readiness records as command, process, GPU, model runtime, job dispatch, credential, network, destructive filesystem, automation, operations-control, or live machine-control permission

& [CanonicalIR7ReadinessChunk] is the post-IR6 implementation chunk record
  + [chunk] is IR7 operations dry-run request simulator planning
  + [chunk_state] is ready_for_final_slice_minting
  + [activation_gate] is IR6 implementation proof accepted
  + [activation_gate] is FSC5 operations safety remains accepted
  + [downstream_implementation_activation_state] is gated_until_IR7_final_planning_acceptance
  + [live_control_authority_state] is blocked_until_separate_source_preserved_SJS_authority

  = must: preserve this order unless completion review rebakes the implementation surface
  = must: mark downstream implementation stale when an upstream accepted output changes

& [CanonicalIR7ReadinessModelRouting] is the model-routing record
  + [IR7_readiness] is requires deeper reasoning for operations manager, job-control simulation, resource-boundary modeling, future dispatch, and live-control safety semantics
  + [IR7_final_slice_minting] is requires deeper reasoning
  + [IR7_boundary_import] is requires deeper reasoning
  + [IR7_dry_run_contract_design] is requires deeper reasoning
  + [IR7_resource_safety_and_refusal_contract] is requires deeper reasoning
  + [IR7_fixture_drafting] is GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark-suitable only after IR7 safety and dry-run contracts are accepted
  + [IR7_future_inert_implementation] is GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark-suitable only after IR7 implementation activation slices are accepted and implementation tasks are bounded
  + [IR7_live_control_reconsideration] is requires deeper reasoning and separate SJS safety authority

  = must: state Spark suitability or deeper-reasoning requirement in every future work packet

& [CanonicalIR7SafetyLimit] is the inherited safety limit for IR7 readiness
  + [operation_request_record_status] is planning_record_only
  + [dry_run_result_record_status] is planning_record_only
  + [human_approval_record_status] is planning_record_only_until_future_authority
  + [refusal_record_status] is planning_record_only
  + [operations_simulator_implementation_authorized] is false
  + [agent_dispatch_authorized] is false
  + [operations_control_authorized] is false
  + [live_machine_control_authorized] is false

  = must: block command execution, process control, GPU control, model runtime mutation, job dispatch, credential access or mutation, network exposure mutation, destructive filesystem action, persistent operations automation, operations control, and live machine control
  = must: prevent dry-run success, fixture success, broad approval, projected intent, mailbox carrier state, or coordination claim state from becoming live-control authority

